  "worked_solution": "A vector-valued function is continuous on an interval if and only if each of its components is continuous on that interval.  \n\nLet's consider the functions one-by-one. \n\n- The function  $p(s)$ is not continuous on $[1,4]$ because \nits second component, $\\frac{s}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061s}$ , is undefined at $s=1$ and hence discontinuous on $[1,4].$\n\n- The function $q(s)$ is continuous on $[1,4]$ because each of its components $s{e}^{s}$, ${s}^{2}{e}^{s}$ and $-\\frac{s}{{e}^{s}}$ are continuous on $[1,4].$\n\n- The function $r(s)$ is continuous on $[1,4]$ because each of its components $\\sqrt{s}$, $2-{s}^{2}$ and $s\\operatorname{ln}\u2061s$ are continuous on $[1,4].$\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n$\\,$ $q(s)$ and $r(s)$ only",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
